# The 3D-Editor under a path of a site served by Caddy 2 (docs/subpath.md): the editor at
# https://example.com/3d/, the embeddable desk at https://example.com/3d/desk.html.
#
# To change: the host name (example.com), the prefix (/3d: in redir, handle_path and
# X-Forwarded-Prefix) and the editor server's address (127.0.0.1:8080). Caddy gets the site's
# certificate by itself; the rest of the site goes in the same site block (see the end).
# {?query} keeps the query of /3d?… in the redirect and needs Caddy 2.9 or later. An older Caddy
# replaces {?query} with nothing, so its redirect drops the query; there, /3d/?{query} keeps the
# query (and redirects /3d to /3d/? when there is none).
# X-Forwarded-Prefix, set here in place of a client's, tells the editor server where it lives and
# that the paths come without /3d: it then removes nothing from them. Set BASE_PATH=/3d on the
# editor server as well (docs/subpath.md). A proxy that keeps the prefix (handle in place of
# handle_path) sends no X-Forwarded-Prefix and drops a client's: header_up -X-Forwarded-Prefix.
#
# Caddy 2.9 or later ({?query}): handle_path strips /3d; the header tells the editor so and its base
example.com {
	redir /3d /3d/{?query} 308
	handle_path /3d/* {
		reverse_proxy 127.0.0.1:8080 {
			header_up X-Forwarded-Prefix /3d
			flush_interval -1
		}
	}

	# the rest of the site, for example:
	# handle {
	# 	root * /srv/www
	# 	file_server
	# }
}
